  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Animal Kingdom Lodge is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants animals right outside the room.</strong> Savanna View rooms look over one of the grazing areas. Even if you book a Resort View or Water View room, you can still walk out to the viewing spots around the lobby and the grounds.</li>
      <li><strong>Families who like having real restaurants at the hotel.</strong> Boma and Jiko are at Jambo House, and Sanaa is a short walk at Kidani Village. You are not limited to a food court.</li>
      <li><strong>Parties of four who don't need a fifth bed.</strong> Standard rooms sleep four. They are on the smaller side for a Deluxe resort, at about 344 sq ft <span class="verify">[verify]</span>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need to sleep five in one hotel room.</strong> A standard room here does not have a day bed. You would need a suite, or a villa next door.</li>
      <li><strong>A short trip to Magic Kingdom is the point of the stay.</strong> This is a bus-only resort. Animal Kingdom is the closest park, and the other three are a longer bus ride.</li>
      <li><strong>You are staying between now and January 2027.</strong> Jambo House guest rooms are under renovation from May 2026 through January 2027. Disney says you may see or hear construction, and that most amenities remain available.</li>
    </ul>
