  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Uzima Springs Pool</strong> at Jambo House is the main pool. Disney lists it at 11,000 square feet and 234,980 gallons, facing Uzima Savanna, with a 67-foot slide, zero-depth entry, and a lounge and bar nearby.</li>
      <li><strong>Samawati Springs Pool</strong> at Kidani Village is a short walk away. Official listings say it is 4,700 square feet and 118,138 gallons, with a 128-foot slide and zero-depth entry. <strong>Uwanja Camp</strong>, next to that pool, is a splash area with zones aimed at younger and older kids.</li>
      <li>Towels are free at the pools. Hours and lifeguard coverage vary and can change.</li>
      <li>The other big activity is the animals. Official pages say more than 200 hoofed animals and birds roam four savannas around the lodge. You can watch from a Savanna View balcony or from the public viewing areas.</li>
    </ul>
