  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Resort View room if the balcony view is not the point.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran from $508 to $915 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. That is the lowest hotel rate at this resort.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay for Savanna View if watching the animals is why you booked.</strong> Savanna View rooms ran about $731 to $1,227. Water View rooms, which look at the pool, ran about $556 to $976.</li>
      <li><strong>Don't book a standard room if you need space for five.</strong> These rooms sleep four. A one-bedroom suite or a villa is the next step up.</li>
      <li><strong>Club Level is a different product.</strong> You are paying for the lounge, usually with a savanna view. Compare that cost with breakfast at Boma or The Mara.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Deluxe rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $35 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>If you are staying through January 2027, read the renovation note before you book a specific view or floor.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
